{"duration_api_ms":117295,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d0f27cd7-0f05-4e02-8215-a5e9a9d1c895","total_cost_usd":0.182226,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16158,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":11759,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6812},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16158,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11759,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16158},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11759,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16158,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.182226,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":6812,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a one-dimensional curve traced by flight-path angle at the corner D≈3.384–3.3852 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg. Flux runs from 227k to 275k W/m2 and bondline temperature from 391 to 418 K. The corner is set by hard limits. Diameter is capped by heatshield mass fraction, which behaves like 1-k·D^2, so the margin hits zero near D≈3.38524. Bluntness is capped near 1.2 by the aero-surface hull, since 1.205, 1.21 and 1.22 all failed. Cone is at its 70 deg bound. Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma and reaches 12 g near -3.570 deg. The last two rounds added only 0.0001 of hypervolume, so the front is saturated. What remains is a small diameter push and filling gaps along the gamma sweep.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-4bd90cfc37e5 (D 3.3851, gamma -3.568) has mass margin 8.6e-5 and g margin 3.2e-4. C-f76375e28006 (D 3.3852) has mass margin 2.7e-5. That gives about 5.9e-5 of margin lost per 1e-4 m of D, so the zero crossing is near D≈3.38524.\",\"C-636b6aeca4e0 (gamma -3.57, D 3.384) has g margin 8e-5, so the g=12 limit is near gamma -3.5705.\",\"C-8efdd90862a0, C-099cae65259a and C-26610a6c01d5 show that lowering bluntness or cone reduces the mass margin and raises flux. Bluntness 1.2 with cone 70 is therefore the best corner.\",\"C-114b79b08144 (D 3.2) has mass margin 0.103. C-fdb02e4f3a4f (D 3.2, b 0.5, cone 45) is infeasible on mass fraction and has flux 425k. Small or slender designs are dominated.\",\"C-de929f2046c9, C-207a027e9dd5 and C-4d9cd4c2b38d show that pushing bluntness above 1.2 fails on hull extrapolation, and C-9c1cc1a27672 and C-f986776067bd show that it also fails on geometry.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heating falls with nose radius (b·D/2) and with lower ballistic coefficient (larger D), so D and b should sit at their caps. Bondline temperature follows heat load, which falls for a steeper and shorter pulse, so gamma should sit just inside the g=12 limit. Flux rises and temperature falls as gamma steepens, which traces the trade-off front. Moving D from 3.384 to 3.38522 gives about 120 W/m2 less flux and about 0.03 K less temperature at fixed gamma. That shifts the whole front very slightly and can only lift hypervolume marginally. Shallow-gamma points at D 3.38522 fill the gaps between the existing front points.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The gains are tiny, of order 1e-4 in normalised hypervolume. The D cap estimate assumes the mass margin is linear in D. If it is not, the D=3.38522 designs could fail the mass constraint by about 1e-5, and they would all fail together. The predicted flux and temperature come from linear interpolation between neighbouring evaluated gammas. The D effect is a correction extrapolated from only three D values. The g margin near -3.570 deg is a few 1e-4 and could flip.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to the estimated mass cap with gamma at the g limit to reach the corner of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5702},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274580,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the exact corner. It may slightly dominate C-636b6aeca4e0 and C-4bd90cfc37e5.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Corner-adjacent point with slightly more g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274460,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.15,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safer fallback near the corner if the -3.5702 point violates g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the gap between -3.545 and -3.56 at the larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274090,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.27,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the upper end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Gap filling between -3.52 and -3.545.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273610,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Gap filling around -3.49, next to the D 3.3851 point at -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.49},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272650,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.87,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Gap filling between -3.4 and -3.52.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.46},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271930,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Gap filling between -3.28 and -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.38},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270020,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.98,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Gap filling at gamma -3.34.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.34},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269050,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4bd90cfc37e5\",\"rationale\":\"Gap filling between -3.05 and -3.22.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38522,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.16},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264710,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.28,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the mid front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"par